(7489563, 1192202, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that contributes to the challenge<br/> <br/>Well, that one shot will certainly give NASA something to think about, a spaceman there already! Your image fills the challenge brief well. I like the backdrop of the space scene it works well. I have to say that I find all the colours too garish, it feels more like a fish tank than a believable space scene. The lighting is a little too harsh with some near-blown highlights. Im sorry if I appear harsh but I hope this may explain your lower than expected score but please do keep at it Martin</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that contributes to the challenge Well, that one shot will certainly give NASA something to think about, a spaceman there already! Your image fills the challenge brief well. I like the backdrop of the space scene it works well. I have to say that I find all the colours too garish, it feels more like a fish tank than a believable space scene. The lighting is a little too harsh with some near-blown highlights. Im sorry if I appear harsh but I hope this may explain your lower than expected score but please do keep at it Martin', '2016-12-30 09:25:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(7489566, 1192322, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that contributes well to the challenge<br/> <br/>Another excellent entry Eugene and justifiably rewarded with a healthy score and placing, well done. In the context of the challenge brief your image works so well. I love the upper part of the image with those lovely shadows and the zoom burst effect, that against the sharp detail of the habitation is a tremendous contrast. The whole thing is utterly believable, lovely colours, just the right amount of blur, love it well done again.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that contributes well to the challenge Another excellent entry Eugene and justifiably rewarded with a healthy score and placing, well done. In the context of the challenge brief your image works so well. I love the upper part of the image with those lovely shadows and the zoom burst effect, that against the sharp detail of the habitation is a tremendous contrast. The whole thing is utterly believable, lovely colours, just the right amount of blur, love it well done again.', '2016-12-30 09:34:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(7489568, 1192274, 114969, '<td valign="top">Flying iguanas ftw! After all, some dinosaurs evolved into birds, so it all sounds logical :) I love your imagination and creativity. Congrats on the ribbon!</td>', 'Flying iguanas ftw! After all, some dinosaurs evolved into birds, so it all sounds logical :) I love your imagination and creativity. Congrats on the ribbon!', '2016-12-30 09:42:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(7489569, 1192277, 114969, '<td valign="top">Using very harsh shadows was such a clever move. It makes things look "space-ish", like if there was no atmosphere to protect the planet. The unusual association of colors also works quite well in that regard. Congratulations Paul on the ribbon!</td>', 'Using very harsh shadows was such a clever move. It makes things look "space-ish", like if there was no atmosphere to protect the planet. The unusual association of colors also works quite well in that regard. Congratulations Paul on the ribbon!', '2016-12-30 09:47:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(7489579, 1192313, 16148, '<td valign="top">A hopeful feeling to this.  Nice way to kick off 2017.</td>', 'A hopeful feeling to this.  Nice way to kick off 2017.', '2016-12-30 10:58:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(7489583, 1192016, 1686, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all who voted and commented.<br/> <br/>I don''t know if there is a formal name for this type of image. Some have called them "small planets" which I like and tend to use when referring to them.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2016-12-30 11:27:37.</i></td>', 'Thanks to all who voted and commented. I don''t know if there is a formal name for this type of image. Some have called them "small planets" which I like and tend to use when referring to them.', '2016-12-30 11:25:31.000000', '2016-12-30 11:27:37.000000', 0),
(7489594, 1192335, 86447, '<td valign="top">I''m glad to see you''re back!    Remember, each election affects the "other side" the same way.   <br/> <br/>I love the floating rock!<br/></td>', 'I''m glad to see you''re back!    Remember, each election affects the "other side" the same way.    I love the floating rock!', '2016-12-30 11:46:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(7489601, 1192322, 114969, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your detailed notes, it is very interesting to see how you actually translated your idea into an image. This kind of planning shows how involved you are in the creative process, so it is no surprise seeing your great entries doing well one after the other. Talent and work at play!</td>', 'Thanks for your detailed notes, it is very interesting to see how you actually translated your idea into an image. This kind of planning shows how involved you are in the creative process, so it is no surprise seeing your great entries doing well one after the other. Talent and work at play!', '2016-12-30 12:08:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(7489604, 1192089, 114969, '<td valign="top">It definitely looks like nothing of our own little planet, great great job creating this! The uncommon landscape along with these strange pink planets would make for a fantastic set, in some space opera movie for example. I love your imagination.</td>', 'It definitely looks like nothing of our own little planet, great great job creating this! The uncommon landscape along with these strange pink planets would make for a fantastic set, in some space opera movie for example. I love your imagination.', '2016-12-30 12:22:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(7489606, 1192335, 114969, '<td valign="top">Nice to see you back at work. I so understand your reaction after the election. That being said, as an artist, this is a good time to translate your thoughts and feelings into images: I am convinced the result would be interesting, and who knows, maybe useful (and not just for you). For what it''s worth, loads of persons in the US and across the world are with you on this one: let''s do our best to overcome this (real) challenge!</td>', 'Nice to see you back at work. I so understand your reaction after the election. That being said, as an artist, this is a good time to translate your thoughts and feelings into images: I am convinced the result would be interesting, and who knows, maybe useful (and not just for you). For what it''s worth, loads of persons in the US and across the world are with you on this one: let''s do our best to overcome this (real) challenge!', '2016-12-30 12:28:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(7489607, 1192318, 114969, '<td valign="top">So very audacious. First of all, I love the angle you chose, although this is a complex one to handle properly in a composite - which you managed perfectly. Then, your choice of colors works beautifully, the rainbow-ish flare is a nice touch, and the glowing effect on the highlights brings the final touch. I say, great work.</td>', 'So very audacious. First of all, I love the angle you chose, although this is a complex one to handle properly in a composite - which you managed perfectly. Then, your choice of colors works beautifully, the rainbow-ish flare is a nice touch, and the glowing effect on the highlights brings the final touch. I say, great work.', '2016-12-30 12:30:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(7489608, 1192264, 61552, '<td valign="top">I hope you saw the humor in this.<br/></td>', 'I hope you saw the humor in this.', '2016-12-30 12:37:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(7489609, 1192332, 114969, '<td valign="top">When I saw the title under the thumbnail, I first was a bit surprised... I mean, "hairballs", "tiny moon", on DPC? ;-) Then I clicked, and smiled at the cuteness. It instantly reminded me Saint-Exupéry''s "Little Prince", and the memories of childhood. Technically, I really like the choice of complementary colors, it makes things pop out so very well! Thanks for the travel :)</td>', 'When I saw the title under the thumbnail, I first was a bit surprised... I mean, "hairballs", "tiny moon", on DPC? ;-) Then I clicked, and smiled at the cuteness. It instantly reminded me Saint-Exupéry''s "Little Prince", and the memories of childhood. Technically, I really like the choice of complementary colors, it makes things pop out so very well! Thanks for the travel :)', '2016-12-30 12:37:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(7489611, 1192071, 114969, '<td valign="top">Why the hell isn''t this on the front page? Great message, great composition, great colors, so very needed in every way. Thanks for this.</td>', 'Why the hell isn''t this on the front page? Great message, great composition, great colors, so very needed in every way. Thanks for this.', '2016-12-30 12:41:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(7489613, 1192016, 30982, '<td valign="top">That''s one heck of a selfie-stick you must have.... :-)  Seriously, where were you to get the shots for this?  (And I call them mini-planets, too - they''re fun but hard to do!)  Well done!</td>', 'That''s one heck of a selfie-stick you must have.... :-)  Seriously, where were you to get the shots for this?  (And I call them mini-planets, too - they''re fun but hard to do!)  Well done!', '2016-12-30 13:01:09.000000', NULL, 0),
